1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:04,807
Welcome to SimpleShell, Team H1's C eleven command interpreter.

2
00:00:04,757 --> 00:00:09,630
Here is the published final release, running live in a clean Ubuntu terminal.

3
00:00:09,630 --> 00:00:11,594
The prompt is ready.

4
00:00:11,594 --> 00:00:14,438
Help lists the supported commands.

5
00:00:14,438 --> 00:00:20,625
P W D reports the current directory; echo preserves this quoted phrase as one argument.

6
00:00:20,625 --> 00:00:25,854
C D changes the shell's directory, and another P W D confirms it.

7
00:00:25,854 --> 00:00:29,374
Input redirection reads the file through less than.

8
00:00:29,374 --> 00:00:34,821
The first echo creates it with greater than; the second appends with double greater than.

9
00:00:34,821 --> 00:00:39,426
Cat then reads back both lines, confirming the file contents.

10
00:00:39,426 --> 00:00:42,959
Here the built-in echo feeds a four-stage pipeline.

11
00:00:42,959 --> 00:00:47,971
T R splits the words, sort orders them, and unique counts duplicates.

12
00:00:47,971 --> 00:00:53,954
The result is the correct count for each color, showing data moving across several processes.

13
00:00:53,954 --> 00:00:58,214
This also verifies that a built-in can run inside a pipeline.

14
00:00:58,214 --> 00:01:05,178
The shell starts sleep with an ampersand, reports the background process, and returns to the prompt immediately.

15
00:01:05,178 --> 00:01:10,535
A follow-up command runs while it works; the shell later reports its completion.

16
00:01:10,535 --> 00:01:14,489
The prompt stays responsive while the background task runs.

17
00:01:14,489 --> 00:01:20,408
An unterminated quote is rejected with a syntax diagnostic before command execution.

18
00:01:20,408 --> 00:01:25,918
The prompt remains available, and this valid echo proves the shell recovers cleanly.

19
00:01:25,918 --> 00:01:30,790
Parser validation rejects the malformed input before a command runs.

20
00:01:30,790 --> 00:01:37,474
Now make test runs the release's parser, executor, integration, and termination suites.

21
00:01:37,474 --> 00:01:47,168
The complete suite also exercises quoting, operator limits, large pipeline transfers, descriptor cleanup, redirection, and background reaping.

22
00:01:47,168 --> 00:01:53,278
The actual run passes: zero failures, including seventy shell integration checks.

23
00:01:53,278 --> 00:01:56,874
SimpleShell, version one point zero final.

24
00:01:56,874 --> 00:01:59,043
Development is frozen.

